# Shrink-only ratchet baseline: fabricated pure-Simple (lib__* / os__*) bodies.
#
# Format: one "<entry-binary-basename> <mangled-symbol>" per line, # comments.
# Read by simpleos_simple_symbol_baseline in
# src/compiler/70.backend/backend/llvm_native_link.spl (channel 3 of
# simpleos_check_no_fabricated_rt_stubs).
#
# CONTRACT
# - This file is SHRINK-ONLY. Entries may be deleted, never added. A new
#   fabricated pure-Simple symbol is a dropped implementation and must fail the
#   link, not be recorded here.
# - A missing file means an EMPTY baseline (maximum strictness), so deleting it
#   can never weaken the gate.
# - Unlike the rt_* side there is no companion allowlist. An rt_* extern can
#   legitimately be an absent backend whose caller reads nil as "unavailable";
#   a pure-Simple function body cannot. Every entry below is a defect.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS (2026-07-28)
# The stub generator fabricates a weak nil-returning definition for ANY symbol
# left undefined in the freestanding link set. The fabrication guard added for
# task #97 was scoped to rt_* only, so lib__* / os__* went unprotected from the
# day it was written. The proven instance was
# ..._simple_web_html_layout_renderer_layout__skip_wrap_spaces in the WM
# production desktop kernel: bound to an 8-byte "xor %eax,%eax; ret" from three
# call sites inside ..._style__parse_font_shorthand_family, while the real body
# sat in the same ELF under the ..._foundation__ prefix. Cause: an object cache
# entry for style.spl compiled BEFORE the function moved modules was reused, so
# it still referenced the pre-move mangled name. Remedy is to purge the stale
# cached objects and rebuild -- which is why that symbol is deliberately NOT
# listed below.
#
# Baseline is intentionally empty. Do not add to it without a written rationale
# in doc/08_tracking/bug/ and a dated removal plan.
